    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23045" root="شمل" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَمِلٌ</span></b>  <i>Wrapping,</i> or <i>inwrapping, himself</i>
(↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُشْتَمِلٌ</span></b> ) <i>with a</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَمْلَة</span> [q. v.]. (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  And
<i>Thin;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَقِيقٌ</span>: thus expl. by Sh, as applied in
this sense by Ibn-Mukbil to a she-camel's tail,
which he terms <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لِيف</span>. (TA.)

